Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 18:48:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07244/11362] [outer-loop] retire ARC public-game solving
 floor: all 25 public games cleared, no more to solve

Operator directive: "now that the registry of public levels is complete, we
should not continue to try and solve them anymore." All 25 public survey
games now show full_game_clear: true in ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml
(reproducible_total_levels: 183, reproducible_total_games: 25).

Retired three CLAUDE.md rules with RETIRED status banners (prose preserved
unedited below each banner, per never-prune):
- ARC-AGI-3 November-Submission Standing Floor (was: >=1 ARC task slot every
  milestone through Nov 2026)
- ARC Level-Up Attempt Guarantee (was: >=1 level-up-bank attempt per
  roadmap, mechanically enforced)
- ARC-AGI-3 Incremental-Progress Scoping (retired for public games only;
  the +1..+n scoping principle is preserved for if a new public game is
  ever added)

Urgent mechanical fix: scripts/arc_levelup_guarantee_lint.py, wired into
research_conductor.py's activation guard (date-gated through 2026-11-01),
required >=1 level-up attempt per roadmap or it hard-refused to activate
the milestone. Left unpatched, the standing autonomous conductor would have
permanently deadlocked on its next planning cycle the moment a planner
correctly stopped proposing dead-end public-game solve tasks -- there is no
longer any level-up attempt it's possible to make. Patched
_all_public_games_cleared() to check the registry first and pass trivially
(with a clear message) once every tracked public game is cleared; fails
open (original enforcement) if the registry is missing/malformed. Verified
against a synthetic zero-ARC-tasks roadmap -- the exact scenario that used
to hard-block -- now passes cleanly.

Also fixed: bp35's registry game-entry was missing the full_game_clear /
final_game_state fields other games get, so reproducible_total_games was
stuck at 24 even after bp35's win landed this session. Corrected to 25.

Updated ops/known-issues.md's live MANDATORY-NEXT-MILESTONE ARC entry with
a matching retirement banner (preserving the ~2000-line historical task
queue below it, per the project's documentation-update discipline).

Updated project memory (project_arc_final_sprint_state.md, badly stale --
was describing a mid-June state) with the current accurate status and an
explicit open question: what, if anything, replaces the retired floor.

